  "description": "YEFLUU crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C86 H92 Fe6 N34 O64 Tb4,C2 H3 N1,2(C1 H2 Cl2),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Tb1F (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2F (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1F (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe2F (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe3F (Fe) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.141-3.833 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.88-131.68°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Fe6Tb4(μ4-O)2(μ3-OH)2(mdea)6(dnbz)8(N3)4]·MeCN·3H2O·2CH2Cl2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
